<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Shoot</h1>
<p>Skill
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>shoot &lt;target&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>shoot rabbit
</pre>
<p>Fires a bow, a crossbow or a sling at someone in the room. Hold the 
weapon (see <a cmd='#'>Help Hold</a>); it takes both hands, so wield nothing else. 
Each needs its own ammunition: arrows for a bow, bolts for a crossbow, 
stones for a sling. You take them from a quiver (or a pouch, for stones) 
that you wear, or else from your inventory. A magical bow needs none: it 
draws on your mana instead.
</p><p>Whether you hit depends on your skill with the weapon (bow, crossbow or 
sling) and your dexterity, against your target's dexterity and wits. A 
hit does the weapon's damage, more if the arrow or bow is made for slaying 
that kind of creature; the arrow is left in the target, or falls to the 
ground. To shoot a player, both of you must have signed the Book of 
Blood.
</p><p>Only the weapon skill counts; the Nymgaard Rangers teach all three 
(see <a cmd='#'>Help Ranger Weapons</a>). Some magic items raise a shoot skill, but 
shooting doesn't use it.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Hold</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Ranger Weapons</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>
</pre>




</div>